   C. write path: wrote 'interactive' back to all 4 core(s) and read 'interactive'
                  back -- writable in fact, and every core agrees on what it read.

== window A -- as installed (every core on 'interactive', nothing written yet)
   busy 0.81 of 4 cores; 38 zone(s) read
   wrote 'performance' to all 4 core(s) and read 'performance' back: the cores are PINNED from
   here until the undo (this is the image's own state -- the second heat cause put back).

== window B -- the cores PINNED (the one change this experiment makes)
   busy 0.54 of 4 cores
   wrote 'interactive' to all 4 core(s) and read 'interactive' back: this is the state it started in.

== the wait -- does window A's reading come back before the control window reads it?
   window A's hottest tsens zone: 49.6 C. Waiting up to 240s (every 10s) for it to come
   back to within 0.5 C of that before window C reads anything.
   IT CAME BACK: 45.4 C after 10s, against window A's 49.6 C (margin 0.5 C). Window C
   below is therefore a CONTROL and not a second reading of the same heat.

== window C -- the CONTROL: the fix's state again, so the third window is the same state as the first
   busy 0.82 of 4 cores
   final state: all 4 core(s) read 'interactive' -- the fix is where this script found it.

